Z||000000||007DOUG||09-03-2001||08:10 AM||||Had some spare fiero parts around, decided to decorate the walls of my garage....what do you think? Art or junk?<P>Pictured below is the GM blueprint for the Indy Logo found in every Indy seat (its signed/approved 1983), along with an authentic Indy doorskin and various fiero awards.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroart1.jpg"> <BR>Pictured below are mint steering wheels from an 84 SE coupe, an Indy, and a GT. Above the wheels are license plates removed from a few of the pace cars I've bought.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroart2.jpg"> <P>I'm working on a fiero "couch". It'll be made from a GT rear clip. I've seen this done with various 50's cars and corvette rear ends.   <P>------------------<BR>4 Indy pace Cars<BR>84 T-top<BR>86 GT Red<BR>86 GT Yellow ASAP<BR>86 GT Blue w/4:10 tranny<BR>86 GT Pearl White 3.4 T-top<BR>88 Formula Red 5 speed<BR>2 Black 88 GT's (twins)<P>However......<BR><I>"Time is my most precious and most perishable of all my possessions."</I>||||reg||6
